"Angular CLI) stiliseret med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"og\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken custom elements\n"
"til Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Udvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hvad er her\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` kalder `registerPantokenElements()` (fra `@pantoken/"
"angular`) én gang ved opstart, så\n"
"  elementer som `<instui-icon>` virker i skabeloner, og importerer token/"
"komponent-CSS plus\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (forbinder modal-, tooltip- og andre "
"komponentadfærder ud af\n"
"  boksen).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` er en standalone-komponent "
"(`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` lader skabelon-compileren\n"
"  acceptere pantoken's custom element-tags) hvis skabelon er stiliseret med "
"`instui-*`\n"
"  klasser; valgfri indsætningspunkter (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"er markeret med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Anvend klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for den komplette "
"klasselist.\n"
"\n"
"## Læs mere\n"
"\n"
"Se [startguiden](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) for at lære "
"mere.\n"

#: canvas-theme-editor/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Upload-ready assets for Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus a local preview "
"for authoring Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) page templates styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload these two files under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** in Canvas.\n"
"  They're built for the CDN provider/theme/mode you chose when scaffolding "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light by default) and include a loader "
"for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up component behaviors like modal, "
"tooltip, and drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — a local, TinyMCE-based editor (`npm run "
"dev`) that mirrors Canvas's\n"
"  RCE so you can author page templates against pantoken's classes before "
"copying them into Canvas.\n"
"  The page itself is built with pantoken's `wrapper` layout: click **Edit "
"theme** to open a tray\n"
"  with **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** tabs (CDN provider/theme/mode selects, "
"and syntax-highlighted,\n"
"  hand-editable copies of `theme.css`/`theme.js` that feed the live "
"preview), and the **?** button\n"
"  for full instructions. Use the **Layouts** toolbar button to start from "
"one of pantoken's bundled\n"
"  starter page layouts (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, "
"testimonial), sourced from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"This opens a Vite dev server with:\n"
"\n"
"- An **editor** pane (TinyMCE, matching the version/config\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) itself "
"uses — see below).\n"
"  Use the **Layouts** button to load one of the bundled starter layouts "
"(this replaces the whole\n"
"  document, after a confirm, rather than inserting at the cursor), and the "
"**Source code** toggle\n"
"  to hand-edit the raw HTML in a syntax-highlighted (CodeMirror) view "
"alongside the editor, with\n"
"  the preview pane updating live as you type — unlike TinyMCE's stock `code` "
"plugin, which edits in\n"
"  a one-shot modal dialog with no live preview.\n"
"- A **preview** pane showing the editor's content with the current CSS/JS "
"tab's stylesheet/script\n"
"  applied (not just the resolved CDN URLs), wrapped to match Canvas's own "
"content-area background\n"
"  and max width — a faithful \"what this will look like once uploaded to "
"Canvas\" check, updated\n"
"  live as you type or edit the theme.\n"
"- The editor and preview panes sit in a split view you can resize by "
"dragging the divider, stack\n"
"  vertically instead of side by side, and swap the order of (drag a pane's "
"toolbar onto the other,\n"
"  or use the **Swap panes** button). Each pane has its own fullscreen "
"button.\n"
"- The **Edit theme** tray's **Config** tab holds the CDN provider/theme/mode "
"selects and\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; its **CSS**/**JS** "
"tabs are editable copies\n"
"  of the generated files — hand-edit them and the preview picks up your "
"changes directly. Changing\n"
"  a Config select re-generates the CSS/JS tabs unless you've already edited "
"them, in which case a\n"
"  **Regenerate from config** button appears instead of silently overwriting "
"your edit.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` and `theme.js` to Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) so\n"
"   pantoken's classes are available on every page.\n"
"2. Run `npm run dev`, use **Layouts** to start from a bundled starter, and "
"edit it like you\n"
"   would in Canvas's own RCE.\n"
"3. Click **Copy HTML** and paste the result into a Canvas page's RCE (switch "
"to the HTML editor\n"
"   view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted HTML server-side — this scaffold "
"doesn't attempt to\n"
"   replicate that, so always verify the pasted result in Canvas (see \"Notes "
"on Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   below).\n"
"\n"
"## Notes on Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"The Canvas Rich Content Editor runs TinyMCE and sanitizes submitted HTML on "
"the server against an\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` in canvas-lms, kept in sync with TinyMCE's "
"own\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). What that allowlist means for "
"templates built here:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, and `aria-*` attributes are "
"allowed on every element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (and inline `style`, e.g. "
"for CSS anchor positioning)\n"
"  **do** survive being pasted and saved, contrary to older guidance in this "
"file. `<script>` tags\n"
"  are always stripped.\n"
"- **RCE-safe pantoken components**: static/display components — alert, view, "
"heading, text, table,\n"
"  a button-as-`<a>` (not a real `<button>`), blockquote. Stick to semantic "
"HTML pantoken already\n"
"  supports (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **RCE-unsafe**: anything from `@pantoken/interactions`'s behavior set — "
"modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, or any other component driven by the native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributes. Those attributes aren't in Canvas's "
"sanitizer allowlist, so\n"
"  the markup survives but the interactive behavior silently breaks the first "
"time the page is\n"
"  saved in Canvas, even with `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"present. Real form\n"
"  elements (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) and "
"inline `<svg>` are\n"
"  stripped outright — none of the bundled starter templates use them.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` loads `@pantoken/interactions` from the CDN, which runs in "
"Canvas's global page scope —\n"
"useful for interactions on pages you build directly in Canvas's RCE with raw "
"HTML edits, but (per\n"
"above) any `popover`/`command`-attribute-driven markup pasted from the RCE "
"preview here won't stay\n"
"interactive once saved.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Uploadklar aktiver til Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus en lokal eksempel "
"til forfatning af Rich Content Editor (RCE)-sideskabeloner designet med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## Hvad der er her\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload disse to filer under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** i Canvas.\n"
"  De er bygget til CDN-provideren/tema/tilstand du valgte ved opskaffering "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light som standard) og inkluderer en "
"loader til\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (forbinder komponentadfærd som modal, tooltip og "
"drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — en lokal, TinyMCE-baseret editor (`npm run "
"dev`) der afspejler Canvas's\n"
"  RCE, så du kan forfatte sideskabeloner mod pantoken's klasser før du "
"kopierer dem til Canvas.\n"
"  Siden selv er bygget med pantoken's `wrapper` layout: klik **Edit theme** "
"for at åbne en bakke\n"
"  med **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** faneblade (CDN-provider/tema/tilstand-"
"vælgere, og syntaksmarkeret,\n"
"  håndedigerbar kopi af `theme.css`/`theme.js` der indfaster den direkte "
"forhåndsvisning), og **?**-knappen\n"
"  til fulde instruktioner. Brug **Layouts** værktøjslinjeknappen til at "
"starte fra en af pantoken's bundlede\n"
"  startsidesidelayouts (hero, callout, to-kolonne, rubric note, "
"testimonial), hentet fra\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Udvikl\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Dette åbner en Vite dev-server med:\n"
"\n"
"- En **editor**-rude (TinyMCE, matchende version/config som\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) selv "
"bruger — se nedenfor).\n"
"  Brug **Layouts**-knappen til at indlæse en af de bundlede starterlayouts "
"(dette erstatter hele\n"
"  dokumentet efter en bekræftelse, snarere end at indsætte ved markøren), og "
"**Source code**-skifte\n"
"  til at håndedigere det rå HTML i en syntaksmarkeret (CodeMirror) visning "
"ved siden af editoren, med\n"
"  forhåndsvisningsruden der opdateres direkte mens du skriver — i modsætning "
"til TinyMCE's standard `code` plugin, som redigerer i\n"
"  en engangsboksdialog uden direkte forhåndsvisning.\n"
"- En **preview**-rude som viser editorens indhold med det aktuelle CSS/JS-"
"faneblds stylesheet/script\n"
"  anvendt (ikke bare de løste CDN-URL'er), pakket for at matche Canvas's "
"eget indholds-områdes baggrund\n"
"  og max-bredde — et troværdigt \"hvordan dette vil se ud når det er "
"uploadet til Canvas\" tjek, opdateret\n"
"  direkte mens du skriver eller redigerer temaet.\n"
"- Editor- og forhåndsvisningsruderne sidder i en delt visning du kan ændre "
"størrelse på ved at trække skillelinjen,\n"
"  stable vertikalt i stedet for side om side, og bytte rækkefølgen af (træk "
"en rudes værktøjslinje til den anden,\n"
"  eller brug **Swap panes**-knappen). Hver rude har sin egen fuldskerm-"
"knap.\n"
"- **Edit theme**-bakken's **Config**-faneblad indeholder CDN-provider/tema/"
"tilstand-vælgere og\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; dets **CSS**/**JS**-"
"faneblade er redigerbar kopi\n"
"  af de genererede filer — håndedigér dem og forhåndsvisningen henter dine "
"ændringer direkte. Ændring af\n"
"  en Config-vælger regenererer CSS/JS-fanebladene medmindre du allerede har "
"redigeret dem, i hvilket tilfælde en\n"
"  **Regenerate from config**-knap dukker op i stedet for at stille "
"overskrive din redigering.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` og `theme.js` til Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) så\n"
"   pantoken's klasser er tilgængelige på hver side.\n"
"2. Kør `npm run dev`, brug **Layouts** til at starte fra en bundlet starter, "
"og rediger det som du\n"
"   ville i Canvas's egen RCE.\n"
"3. Klik **Copy HTML** og indsæt resultatet i en Canvas-sides RCE (skift til "
"HTML-editoren\n"
"   visning først). Canvas saniterer indsatte HTML server-side — dette "
"stilladser forsøger ikke at\n"
"   kopiere det, så verificer altid det indsatte resultat i Canvas (se "
"\"Noter om Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   nedenfor).\n"
"\n"
"## Noter om Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"Canvas Rich Content Editor kører TinyMCE og saniterer indsendt HTML på "
"serveren mod en\n"
"tilladelsesliste (`gems/canvas_sanitize` i canvas-lms, holdt i "
"synkronisering med TinyMCE's egen\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). Hvad denne tilladelsesliste "
"betyder for skabeloner bygget her:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role` og `aria-*` attributter er tilladt "
"på hvert element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (og inline `style`, f.eks. "
"til CSS anker-positionering)\n"
"  **gør** overleve at blive indsatte og gemt, i modsætning til ældre "
"vejledning i denne fil. `<script>` tags\n"
"  fjernes altid.\n"
"- **RCE-sikre pantoken-komponenter**: statiske/display-komponenter — alert, "
"view, heading, text, table,\n"
"  en knap-som-`<a>` (ikke en rigtig `<button>`), blockquote. Hold dig til "
"semantisk HTML pantoken allerede\n"
"  understøtter (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, overskrifter, lister, "
"tabeller).\n"
"- **RCE-usikker**: noget fra `@pantoken/interactions`'s adfærdssæt — modal, "
"tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, eller enhver anden komponent drevet af det native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributter. Disse attributter er ikke i Canvas's "
"sanitizer tilladelsesliste, så\n"
"  markeringen overlever men den interaktive adfærd bryder stumme første gang "
"siden\n"
"  gemmes i Canvas, selv med `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader til "
"stede. Rigtige form\n"
"  elementer (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) og "
"inline `<svg>` er\n"
"  fjernet helt — ingen af de bundlede starter-skabeloner bruger dem.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` indlæser `@pantoken/interactions` fra CDN'en, som køres i "
"Canvas's globale sidescope —\n"
"nyttigt til interaktioner på sider du bygger direkte i Canvas's RCE med rå "
"HTML-redigeringer, men (pr.\n"
"ovenstående) enhver `popover`/`command`-attribut-drevet markup indsatte fra "
"RCE-forhåndsvisningen her forbliver ikke\n"
"interaktiv når den gemmes.\n"

#: components/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A plain TypeScript app (via Vite) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructure's\n"
"design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` holds the actual page markup — a `wrapper`-layout shell from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). View source\n"
"  and edit it directly; nothing is injected by JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` imports `@pantoken/css` (defines every `--instui-*` custom "
"property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (document defaults + focus ring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` classes), `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, "
"and other component\n"
"  behaviors out of the box), and your own `src/style.css` — add interactive "
"behavior here.\n"
"- Optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) are marked "
"with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` in `index.html` — replace their contents with "
"your own markup.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [HTML guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En simpel TypeScript-app (via Vite) stilet med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructures\n"
"design tokens og ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Udvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hvad er her\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` indeholder det faktiske sidemarkup — en `wrapper`-layout skal "
"fra\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). Se kildekoden\n"
"  og rediger den direkte; intet indsprøjtes af JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` importerer `@pantoken/css` (definerer hver `--instui-*` "
"brugerdefineret egenskab),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (dokumentstandards + fokusring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` klasser), `@pantoken/interactions` (aktiverer modal, tooltip "
"og andre komponentadfærd som standard), og din egen `src/style.css` — tilføj "
"interaktiv adfærd her.\n"
"- Valgfrie indsætningspunkter (overskrift, filtre, indhold, slutning) er "
"markeret med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` i `index.html` — erstat deres indhold med dit "
"eget markup.\n"
"- Anvend klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for den komplette "
"klasselist.\n"
"\n"
"## Læs mere\n"
"\n"
"Se [HTML-vejledningen](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) for at lære "
"mere.\n"

#: next/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A Next.js (App Router) app styled with [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructure's design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wraps the config with `withPantoken(...)` (adds pantoken "
"to\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` imports `@pantoken/css`, which defines every `--instui-*` "
"custom\n"
"  property, at the root so it's available on every page, plus the `wrapper` "
"layout's root class on\n"
"  `<body>` and `PantokenInteractions` (a client component that loads "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  wires up modal, tooltip, and other component behaviors out of the box).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` renders markup styled with `instui-*` classes; optional "
"insertion points (header,\n"
"  filters, content, trailing) are marked with `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En Next.js (App Router)-app udformet med [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructures designtokens og ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Udvikling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Hvad finder du her\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` omslutter konfigurationen med `withPantoken(...)` "
"(tilføjer pantoken til\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` importerer `@pantoken/css`, som definerer hver `--instui-"
"*` brugerdefineret\n"
"  egenskab, ved roden, så den er tilgængelig på hver side, samt `wrapper` "
"layoutets rodklasse på\n"
"  `<body>` og `PantokenInteractions` (en klientkomponent, der indlæser "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
